  "answer_text": "Here is a complete summary of the **MLA and MP seats in Telangana**:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f MLA Seats (State Legislature)\n\n### 1. Legislative Assembly (Vidhan Sabha)\n- There are **119 MLAs** in the Telangana Legislative Assembly, elected by the people. The state is divided into **119 constituencies** with roughly equal populations.\n- The Telangana Legislative Assembly came into existence with 119 seats in **June 2014** with the formation of Telangana.\n\n### 2. Legislative Council (Vidhan Parishad)\n- The Legislative Council has **40 members**, of whom 14 are elected by members of the Telangana Legislative Assembly, 14 by local authorities of the state, 6 nominated by the Governor, 3 elected by teachers, and 3 elected by graduates of the state.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfdf\ufe0f MP Seats (Parliament)\n\n### 1. Lok Sabha (Lower House)\n- Telangana has **17 Lok Sabha constituencies**, with **3 reserved for Scheduled Castes (SC)** and **2 for Scheduled Tribes (ST)**.\n\n### 2. Rajya Sabha (Upper House)\n- Telangana has **7 Rajya Sabha seats**.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcca Quick Summary Table\n\n| House | Type | Total Seats |\n|---|---|---|\n| Vidhan Sabha | State (MLA) | 119 |\n| Vidhan Parishad | State (MLC) | 40 |\n| Lok Sabha | Parliament (MP) | 17 |\n| Rajya Sabha | Parliament (MP) | 7 |\n| **Total** | | **183** |",
